From 7ba463c8e448c9f85c8a24e69e60b03553dd418d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 18:35:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] RoCEnante: relay opposite-rank payloads over a four-node ring

Base: 236ddff04a5f5064084b46464800b70b34ec7d8c plus deployment B12X patches 0001-0005.

Rationale: direct-peer writes cannot reach the opposite rank of a switchless ring. Explicit ring4 mode connects neighbours only, forwards the completed predecessor payload clockwise, and retains the original receive-slot identity. Protocol ABI 5 validates mode and geometry before connection. Direct mode remains the default.

Quality: GPU kernels, buffer layout and reduction order are unchanged. Mixed modes, overwritten relay slots, excessive payloads and blocked relay waits fail. No extra GPU staging allocation. No hardware or performance claim.

Tests: real proxy C under simulated ordered verbs with ASan/UBSan; 10000 collective rounds across direct3/ring4, one/two stripes, delayed DMA, variable payload sizes, two pending doorbells, sequence wrap and stop/error paths. CPU resolver tests. Four-Spark GPU/RDMA qualification remains pending.

Upstream status: experimental local patch, not submitted.
